==Old English==

===Etymology===
{{proto|Germanic|fedwōr|lang=ang}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|kʷetwóres|lang=ang}}.

Common Germanic cognates include Old High German [[fior]] (German ''[[vier]]''), Old Saxon [[fiuwar]] (Dutch ''[[vier]]''), Old Norse ''[[fjórir]]'', Gothic {{l|got|𐍆𐌹𐌳𐍅𐍉𐍂}}.

Indo-European cognates include {{proto|Slavic|title=Common Slavic|četiri|lang=}} (Russian {{l|ru|четыре}}), Old Irish [[cethair]], Greek {{term|τέσσαρες|lang=grc}}, Latin ''[[quattuor]]''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈfeːower/|lang=ang}}

